[Start "short-system 1...c6"]

2. d3 d5 { Takes the centre at once. White has played a slow move, so Black can claim space. } 3. Nd2 ( 3. exd5 cxd5 { Recaptures towards the centre. With White's pawn only on d3, Black can build a big centre with ...Nc6 and ...e5. } 4. Nf3 ( 4. d4 Nc6 ) ( 4. g3 Nc6 ) ( 4. Nc3 Nf6 ) 4... Nc6 { Develops and covers d4 and e5. } 5. g3 ( 5. d4 Bg4 { Pins the knight that guards d4. White has spent two moves on the d-pawn, so Black is a move ahead of the Exchange Variation. } ) 5... e5 { Two pawns side by side on d5 and e5 give Black the centre. } 6. Bg2 Nf6 ) ( 3. Nf3 Bg4 4. h3 ( 4. Be2 e6 { Supports d5 and keeps the pin. Black develops with ...Nf6 and ...Bd6 or ...Be7, and can swap on f3 when it suits. } ) ( 4. exd5 cxd5 ) ( 4. Nbd2 e6 ) ( 4. Nc3 { The same position as 2.Nc3 d5 3.Nf3 Bg4 4.d3: Black plays ...e6. } ) 4... Bxf3 5. Qxf3 e6 ) ( 3. e5 Bf5 { Out before ...e6, as in the Advance Variation. White's e5 pawn has no d4 pawn behind it, so ...e6 and ...c5 will put it under pressure. } ) ( 3. Nc3 { The same position as 2.Nc3 d5 3.d3: Black plays ...e5. } ) ( 3. f3 e5 { Takes the centre. The pawn on f3 has taken the best square from White's king's knight. } ) 3... e5 { Builds a big pawn centre. White's knight on d2 blocks the bishop, so White cannot easily hit the centre. } 4. Ngf3 Bd6 { Defends e5 and develops. } 5. g3 ( 5. d4 exd4 6. Bd3 Ne7 ) 5... Nf6 { Develops with an attack on e4. } 6. Bg2 O-O { King safe, and the rook goes to e8 next to back up the centre. } 7. O-O Re8 { Adds a defender to e5 and keeps the pressure on e4. Black has a big centre. If White varies, castle and keep the pawns on e5 and d5. } *
